/ Where the car charged, from its position or from the address, over the
  whole width of the form. The user moves its point to the station. Only a
  point with an address and with Nominatim moves, because the build writes
  the other positions (see ChargingSession::Location). On a wide
  screen it takes the height that the window leaves, so the form fits a small
  laptop. Without a position, the space stays, so the form does not jump when
  the address-lookup controller shows the map. The space names the error of
  the address, which the field leaves to it (see the partial address).
#charging_session_map class=['flex h-56 lg:h-[clamp(8rem,100dvh-42rem,20rem)] overflow-hidden rounded-xl', ('items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 text-center text-sm text-muted bg-fill' unless charging_session.location)] data-address-lookup-target='map' data-action='car--map--component:moved->address-lookup#move'
  - if charging_session.location
    / A live map, also when the point does not move: one marker, without a tooltip
    = render Car::Map::Component.new(cars: [{ places: [[*charging_session.location, 1]] }], live: true, movable: charging_session.position_of_address?)
  - elsif charging_session.errors[:address].any?
    = icon 'location-dot', class: 'text-signal-negative'
    span.text-signal-negative#charging_session_map_message = charging_session.errors.full_messages_for(:address).to_sentence
  - else
    = icon 'location-dot'
    = t('charging_sessions.map_empty')
